   "width": "Cell target width: the dominant driver of size features (area, diameter) and the strongest single contributor to eccentricity; much of its effect on area is interaction-borne (large ST-S1).",
   "temp": "Membrane fluctuation temperature: minor across the board; a small direct effect on eccentricity only.",
   "contact": "Homotypic contact energy: moderate driver of perimeter, solidity and circularity via boundary shape.",
   "neighbor": "Neighbour-order radius: negligible for every feature (S1 and ST near zero).",
   "contact_no": "Non-specific contact energy: a modest, mostly interaction-mediated contributor to area/diameter.",
   "lambda": "Volume-constraint stiffness (lambda): secondary size driver of area and diameter, largely through interactions.",
   "cm_adhesion": "Cell-matrix adhesion: the dominant shape driver - controls solidity, perimeter and circularity almost single-handedly."
